
What is string?
=> String is an object of String class that represents a string of characters.
       Example. "Laptop" is a String 6 Characters.



Why need String?
=> String class is used to create a string object.
   It is a predefined immutable class that is present in java.lang package.
   But in Java, all classes are also considered as a data type.

   - Immutable means it cannot be changed.



How to achive String?
=> To handle string data in Java, we need an object of string class. Basically,
   there are three ways to create a string object in Java.

   By string literal.
   By new keyword.
   By converting character arrays into strings



